# deep role-research provider — the REAL ResearchProvider (N3 fast-follow) — apply ladder

2026-05-31. Roadmap N3 fast-follow (fork D-5 (a)) per
`docs/plans/deep-role-research-provider.md`. Fills the seam N3 sealed
(`framework/workspace-bootstrap/src/loam/workspace_bootstrap/deep_role_research.py`,
SEAL 96aae8a): the deep role-research PASS itself (the baseline shipped
ONLY the opt-in gate + the featherlight stub seam).

The slice: given a user's role + their explicit opt-in (both already
established by the sealed intake — this slice NEVER re-gates), run a
BOUNDED three-axis research pass — (i) what makes someone EFFECTIVE at
the role, (ii) what gets people PROMOTED, (iii) which EXISTING AI tools
loam could wrap or rebuild — then SYNTHESIZE a SHORT, person-specific set
of <=3 leverage ideas and return the sealed RoleResearchResult with
is_stub=False, which the intake's as_leverage_ideas() fold-back consumes
UNCHANGED.

The central stance: the synthesis IS the deliverable, not the research.
The user who reaches this seam is — by the sealed intake's routing — at
the bottom of the idea-quality continuum (already overwhelmed). The
over-reach guard therefore applies TWICE: the research runs on a HARD
fixed budget (~3 round-trips, NOT an unbounded agent loop), and the
output is a FEW person-specific ideas (NOT a citation dump that
re-overwhelms).

The LOAD-BEARING finding (plan §10.1): WebSearch/WebFetch/the Agent tool
are Claude-Code SESSION tools, NOT importable functions a standalone
Python provider can call; and loam forbids the Anthropic SDK / API key
(feedback_no_anthropic_api_key). So "compose the forked-research-subagent"
resolves to a bounded `claude -p` subprocess — the subprocess IS a Claude
session with the web-research toolset — spawned through the MANDATED
loam_spawn_isolation.spawn_isolated_claude primitive (--strict-mcp-config
+ empty mcpServers + token/API-key-scrubbed env) so it cannot steal the
operator's Telegram bot slot
(feedback_spawned_claude_must_isolate_telegram_plugin).
loam_spawn_isolation is not a workspace-bootstrap dependency; the provider
LAZY-imports it inside the dispatch and DEGRADES GRACEFULLY when it (or the
claude binary) is absent (AC.DRRGRACE.1) — the same convention the
README_3 outcome-altitude test uses.

